158	1324,687,1540,1274	158. Plan of a Stamen.	The summit of a leaf, with midrib and veins, placed above a short filament bearing an anther whose upper half is cut away to show its two cells full of pollen.
159	1606,617,1737,1274	Fig. 159.	The whole stamen of a Lily: a long slender filament bearing a long anther at its top, with pollen scattered beside it.
